#: README.md
msgid "data-platform-blueprint"
msgstr ""

#: README.md
msgid "A reference architecture for the governed data platform behind an education management information system (EMIS), written so that the architecture stays fixed while the implementation varies. It covers the resources an EMIS holds (learners, schools, teachers and staff, enrolment, attendance, assessment and the indicators reported from them) through operational databases, a lakehouse, governance and access, reporting, backfill and migration, and example products that exercise all of them."
msgstr ""

#: README.md
msgid "Each part of the architecture is a **capability** with a **contract** of numbered, testable clauses that name no vendor. An **implementation** binds each capability to real components and shows evidence for every clause. Two reference implementations are planned: one fully open source on Kubernetes, one on Databricks."
msgstr ""

#: README.md
msgid "Status: blueprint 0.5.0, with 41 capabilities and 246 clauses. Contracts are drafted; no implementation has evidence yet."
msgstr ""

#: README.md
msgid "**New here?** Start with [getting started]{1}: it gives a reading order for everyone and a track for each role."
msgstr ""

#: README.md
msgid "How the blueprint changes"
msgstr ""

#: README.md
msgid "Anyone can propose a change as a **LumenOSS Improvement Proposal (LIP)**: a numbered document that moves in the open from Draft through Review and a 14-day Last Call to a decision, in the manner of the IETF's RFCs, Python's PEPs, Bitcoin's BIPs, Ethereum's EIPs and Cardano's CIPs. Every proposal states its effect on learners' data. Accepted LIPs are recorded as decision records and released in a catalogue version. Read [LIP-1]{1} for the process and start from the [template]{2}. [CONTRIBUTING.md]{3} says which changes need a LIP and which are ordinary reviewed changes, how to set up, and what review looks for."
msgstr ""

